{
  "title": "Bone Signaling & RANKL",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9010/bone-signaling-and-rankl",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 27 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Bone metabolism is a dynamic process that balances bone formation and bone resorption",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "central to this process is the **RANK/RANKL/OPG pathway**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**bone formation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "performed by stimulating osteoblasts and inhibiting osteoclasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**bone resorption**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "performed by active osteoclast",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "stimulated by **RANKL in normal process**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "stimulated by **PTHrP in pathologic process** (metastatic disease)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Osteoblast Signaling in RANKL pathway",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteoblasts produce",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**RANKL**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "binds RANK and stimulates osteoclastic bone resorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**osteoprotegerin (OPG)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inhibits osteoclast differentiation, fusion, and activation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decoy receptor produced by osteoblasts and stromal cells that binds to and sequesters RANKL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "alkaline phosphatase",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Osteoclast Inhibition",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteoclast Inhibition decreases bone resorption",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Molecules that inhibit bone resorption",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**osteoprotegerin (OPG)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**calcitonin**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**interacts directly with the osteoclast via cell-surface receptors**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**estrogen** (via decrease in RANKL)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stimulates bone production (anabolic) and prevents resorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inhibits activation of adenylyl cyclase",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**transforming growth factor beta (TGF beta)** (via increase in OPG)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**interleukin 10 (IL-10)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "suppresses osteoclasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Osteoclast Activation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteoclast activation stimulates bone resorption",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Molecules that stimulate bone resorption**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**RANKL**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "RANKL (ligand) is secreted by osteoblasts and binds to the RANK receptor on osteoclast precursor and mature osteoclast cells",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**PTH**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "activation of its receptor stimulates adenylyl cyclase",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "binds to cell-surface receptors on osteoblasts to stimulate production of RANKL and M-CSF",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**interleukin 1 (IL-1)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stimulates osteoclast differentiation and thus bone resorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**1,25 dihydroxy vitamin D**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stimulates RANKL expression",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**prostaglandin E2**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "activates adenylyl cyclase and stimulates resorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**IL-6 (myeloma)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**MIP-1A (myeloma)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Clinical Implications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Osteoporosis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can result from loss of function of the OPG gene, leading to constitutive activation of osteoclasts which results in uncontrolled bone resorption and ultimately leads to osteoporosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Osteopetrosis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9010/images/osteopetrosis.jpg",
              "caption": "X-ray showing osteopetrosis in skeletally immature patient"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "condition caused by a genetic defect resulting in absence of osteoclastic bone resorption",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "a mouse RANKL knockout model creates a osteopetrosis-like condition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Paget disease**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "felt to be caused by alterations in cytoplastmic binding to RANK or mutations in the OPG gene",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Osteolytic bone metastasis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "found to be mediated by the RANK and RANKL pathway",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "RANKL is produced directly by the cancer cells",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "blocking of RANKL by OPG results in decreased skeletal metastasis in animal models",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bisphosphonates decrease skeletal events in cancer metastasis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Osteolysis following joint arthroplasty**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9010/images/osteolysis.jpg",
              "caption": "X-ray showing left hip osteolysis with eccentric wear."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "polyethylene wear debris is phagocytized by macrophage leads to activation of the macrophage",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "additional macrophages are recruited with release of additional cytokines including RANKL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "RANKL activates osteoclasts which leads to bone resorption around implants",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
